sub_questions.text:
The electric field of a uniform plane electromagnetic wave in free space is $1\text{ volt/metre}$ and frequency is $300\text{ MHz}$. If a very large thick flat copper plate is placed normal to the direction of wave propagation, determine—
(i) $\vec{E}$ and $\vec{H}$ at the surface of plate;
(ii) depth of penetration;
(iii) conduction current density at the surface;
(iv) conduction current density at a distance of $0.01\text{ mm}$ below the surface;
(v) linear current density, $J_s$;
(vi) surface impedance;
(vii) power loss per square metre of surface area.
[Take : $\sigma_{cu} = 5.8 \times 10^7\text{ S/m}$.]
